	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["7A00F7E4F256E45A"]
			description: ["Every hot ingot in the vacuum freezer throws half its liquid helium away. The &6Helium Refrigerator&r keeps a charge in its own hatch and only tops it up. Liquid nitrogen for the precooling, and an IV vacuum freezer line to relieve. Frozen ingots at a fraction of the helium, and the helium your later cryogenics will want. The nitrogen leaves as gas: pipe it back to the Moon's cryogenic plant and let ME top up the helium."]
			icon: "gtceu:helium_refrigerator"
			id: "1368397CE117ECD1"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "51143C2CFF164BCA", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 4, id: "32DEC6633BEFD989", item: "gtceu:liquid_nitrogen_bucket", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "1C61E246579AA5DD", item: "gtceu:helium_refrigerator", type: "item" }]
			title: "Closed Loop"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A00F7E4F256E45A"]
			description: ["GregTech's sterile chain normally waits for a ZPM cleanroom. The &6Biofoundry&r is a sealed hall with an airlock and a UV ceiling, and it runs the whole chain at LuV. Meat and bone from your creature simulators to start with, and a lot of patience for what comes after. Collagen, gelatin and agar from nothing alive. Everything after them needs bacteria, and Earth has none you can use. Feed the simulators by ME and let the sludge it hands back go round again."]
			icon: "gtceu:biofoundry"
			id: "3B64E8E2A5FD37A0"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "3ABC85FC87C82788", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 16, id: "33AF14918A101674", item: "minecraft:bone", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5DA2D5A6129F14AA", item: "gtceu:biofoundry", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5110D841416DB276", item: "gtceu:gelatin_dust", type: "item" }
				{ id: "588877DE57E0E365", item: "gtceu:agar_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Biofoundry"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1F4E8B2F7895A2B7"]
			description: ["The &6Coated Conductor Line&r rolls nickel and Mars tungsten into a textured tape, then lays a film of ITBTC on it with a laser, oxygen and a silver cap. The LuV mixer for the ITBTC dust, and tungsten from the Red Planet. Superconducting tape with no ultra-hot EBF, no helium, and a fraction of the superconductor a cast wire eats. The tape can't be melted back down, so keep a stock and make what the magnet works eats."]
			icon: "gtceu:coated_conductor_line"
			id: "3A6139E43FC0C489"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "15BD08175D0C400B", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 16, id: "362792BD9DE36BAA", item: "gtceu:nickel_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "120E1B3D50FBF348", item: "gtceu:coated_conductor_line", type: "item" }]
			title: "Tape"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3A6139E43FC0C489"]
			description: [
				"The &6ITBTC Coated Conductor&r is the line you built, finished: a nickel-tungsten ribbon wearing a ceramic film that superconducts at a temperature liquid nitrogen reaches."
				"Ship it to the magnet works."
			]
			icon: "grindless:itbtc_coated_conductor"
			id: "1D90C22797563D9A"
			rewards: [{ id: "35877FBCC5CD71DD", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3122AC6EB8A05065", item: "grindless:nickel_tungsten_tape", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7140F7EB4398C2EE", item: "grindless:itbtc_coated_conductor", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Coated and Cut"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7585FE5E7EF942A7"]
			description: ["The &6HTS Magnet Works&r winds tape round a mandrel, soaks it in epoxy and tests it cold before anything leaves the building. Tape from the coated line, epoxy, and a sliver of the trinium GregTech's own coil asks for. The superconducting coil, and with it a fusion ring that LuV can afford. It also winds the network cells, coilgun coils and magnetic bearings. Keep tape and epoxy flowing by ME and the coils stock themselves."]
			icon: "gtceu:hts_magnet_works"
			id: "38F8454E1AEB4E72"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "1E5784757E175F5D", type: "xp", xp: 120 }
				{ count: 2, id: "7C80948DC6AE621F", item: "gtceu:epoxy_bucket", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5D111C4051210281", item: "gtceu:hts_magnet_works", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1A82B4FDD8759FA8", item: "gtceu:superconducting_coil", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Winding"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["38F8454E1AEB4E72"]
			description: [
				"A &6LuV SMES Cell&r keeps its energy in a superconducting coil's field. The bank only hands out LuV once every formed tower holds LuV cells, so swap them all: one forgotten tower in the corner holds the whole network back."
				"Until then, two IV wireless hatches on a multiblock still reach LuV."
			]
			icon: "grindless:luv_smes_cell"
			id: "5933ADF51C8949BD"
			rewards: [{ id: "7376D9A25EC1B869", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "58A6EF8140058C59", item: "grindless:luv_smes_cell", type: "item" }
				{ id: "19853885579FA26A", item: "gtceu:luv_wireless_energy_hatch", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "The Network Goes LuV"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["75745AD963ECB5C8"]
			description: ["Up here the Sun never sets, and the &6Orbital Solar Station&r makes the most of it: two wings of panels on a truss, and every panel that sees open sky pays. Orbital solar panels and station truss casing, then a LuV wireless dynamo hatch to send the power home. Free power on the network. It burns nothing, so nothing doubles it. Panels never wear out, so build it once and let the network sell the surplus."]
			icon: "gtceu:orbital_solar_station"
			id: "3F2030C8DDEDB9FF"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "39623E31E54F56E3", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 2, id: "18F7447DC3B656EE", item: "gcyr:photovoltaic_cell", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7DCDEB7079BC07A6", item: "gtceu:orbital_solar_station", type: "item" }
				{ id: "32FE0E13005F7F83", item: "grindless:orbital_solar_panel", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Endless Day"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["75745AD963ECB5C8"]
			description: ["On the ground ZBLAN glass crystallizes while it's drawn; up here it stays clear. The &6Microgravity Smelter&r draws it into optical pipe with no silver at all. ZBLAN dust, mixed at home in the Large Mixing Vessel because a normal mixer can't hold that much fluorine. Optical pipe for the research station, Whipple shield casing by foaming metal, and naquadah alloy melted floating in a field. Send ZBLAN up by ME and let the pipe come back down the same way."]
			icon: "gtceu:microgravity_smelter"
			id: "121BEE9B7E15DE8C"
			rewards: [{ id: "3FF36420AFEFE3A2", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "36718AA56A92385A", item: "gtceu:microgravity_smelter", type: "item" }
				{ id: "135209E83A9A320B", item: "gtceu:zblan_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Fibre from Nothing"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["121BEE9B7E15DE8C"]
			description: ["A strand of ZBLAN with no crystals in it carries light a long way. This is the &6Optical Pipe&r the research station and the HPCA both wire up with."]
			icon: "gtceu:normal_optical_pipe"
			id: "3504AC546284B5BC"
			rewards: [{ id: "71E81738C368F7A0", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "33A0290EF2E276C2", item: "gtceu:normal_optical_pipe", type: "item" }]
			title: "Clear Glass"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3504AC546284B5BC"]
			description: ["A thin skin of foamed metal, spaced from the hull, turns a micrometeorite into harmless vapour. The smelter foams the &6Whipple Shield Casing&r; the wake facility's disc is made of it."]
			icon: "grindless:whipple_shield_casing"
			id: "76E167FD4B94F42F"
			rewards: [{ id: "5469400217EE3AAE", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "54EA2123B00168F9", item: "grindless:whipple_shield_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Whipple Shield"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["76E167FD4B94F42F"]
			description: ["Behind a disc flying through orbit, the vacuum is emptier than any chamber you could build. The &6Wake Shield Facility&r grows its wafers there. A disc of Whipple shield casing, so the smelter goes first, and the same sources GregTech's own cleanroom asks for. HPIC and UHPIC wafers with half the source and half the time. Give it germanium and it grows solar wafers too. Let ME fill the sources and carry the wafers to the cleanroom."]
			icon: "gtceu:wake_shield_facility"
			id: "58EFB73E6DD24BDB"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "5917C4380DC0402D", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 4, id: "3AEEC37901F33633", item: "gtceu:indium_gallium_phosphide_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "54780AE195859BCD", item: "gtceu:wake_shield_facility", type: "item" }]
			title: "In the Wake"
			x: 8.0d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["58EFB73E6DD24BDB"]
			description: ["The &6UHPIC Wafer&r is the purest slice of silicon the pack makes. Nothing on the ground grows one this clean, and the ZPM chips will be cut from it."]
			icon: "gtceu:uhpic_wafer"
			id: "5D20D0252114492B"
			rewards: [{ id: "5D2ED935CBC7767E", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "52493E94E20E7A74", item: "gtceu:uhpic_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Cleaner than Clean"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["75745AD963ECB5C8"]
			description: ["With nothing stirring the melt, a crystal grows without flaws. The &6Zero-G Crystal Grower&r makes raw crystal chips every time instead of now and then. The same dopant GregTech asks for, and sapphire test masses cut from its own boules. The crystal circuit chain in the circuits chapter, much faster. The test masses are for later; EMI says what for. One grower, one ME bus for dopant, and the chips arrive on their own."]
			icon: "gtceu:zero_g_crystal_grower"
			id: "18A794C8BAA71D81"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "79A3343DDCAA87FC", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 16, id: "70CB42BE6A87A4A8", item: "gtceu:sapphire_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "36BE5E6C87916B16", item: "gtceu:zero_g_crystal_grower", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5132B223B09F2DD4", item: "grindless:sapphire_test_mass", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Perfect Crystal"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F943A5682742ECD"]
			description: ["The belt's veins answer to one drill: the &6Harpoon Anchor Drill&r, pinned to the rock by harpoons while its HSS-S bit works. Bits and harpoons, which both wear slowly. No drilling fluid: it is vacuum, same as Mercury. Raw meteoric iron and the rest of the belt veins. A lathe and a press keep bits and harpoons in stock by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:harpoon_anchor_drill"
			id: "7C258E5E568EE8F2"
			rewards: [{ id: "7591EE6013028AF0", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "58ED6E6D577F6699", item: "gtceu:harpoon_anchor_drill", type: "item" }]
			title: "Harpoon"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C258E5E568EE8F2"]
			description: ["The &6HSS-S Drill Bit&r wears down a little with every bore, and the &6Anchor Harpoon&r stays in the rock until you pull it. Keep spares of both."]
			icon: "grindless:hss_s_drill_bit"
			id: "5F2EEA315A9E5CB3"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "351B287792B112D7", type: "xp", xp: 60 }
				{ count: 2, id: "36A0522C5471B73C", item: "grindless:anchor_harpoon", type: "item" }
			]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "533C0813A5B92E29", item: "grindless:hss_s_drill_bit", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5792BD7C26385D0D", item: "grindless:anchor_harpoon", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Bits and Harpoons"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5F2EEA315A9E5CB3"]
			description: ["The &6Asteroid Processor&r runs the Mond process: carbon monoxide carries the iron and nickel away as gas and leaves the platinum metals behind as a concentrate. Carbon monoxide, which stays in the machine, and meteoric iron from the harpoon drill. The concentrate exists nowhere else, so the processor won't void it. It also pulls tetrataenite apart by magnet. The meteoric iron dust that leaves goes back through Mond; close that loop with ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:asteroid_processor"
			id: "5556DFCD2B6DD947"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "3E232CC68F44C448", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 2, id: "162392BFEE00E911", item: "gtceu:carbon_monoxide_bucket", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "1C58AD65259FF192", item: "gtceu:asteroid_processor", type: "item" }]
			title: "Mond"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5556DFCD2B6DD947"]
			description: ["The &6Rotating Hydroponic Ring&r spins for gravity, keeps the Sun on all the time and seals engineered crops away from the wild. A hub on magnetic bearings of tetrataenite from the processor, wound at the magnet works, and the engineered seeds from home. Neurotrophic factor from the barley and collagen from the tobacco. Neither seed gets eaten. Let ME replant nothing: the ring replants for you. Just drain the factor."]
			icon: "gtceu:hydroponic_ring"
			id: "569ED410C9F7ED07"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "7BBFDF8C1CE6C8A4", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 4, id: "5DFAA661A5D85B49", item: "gtceu:carbon_dioxide_bucket", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "3030C275B47F38E4", item: "gtceu:hydroponic_ring", type: "item" }]
			title: "Molecular Farm"
			x: 8.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["569ED410C9F7ED07"]
			description: ["The ring turns on &6Magnetic Bearings&r, so nothing touches and nothing wears. Make a few spare ones at the magnet works."]
			icon: "grindless:magnetic_bearing"
			id: "564E7FD4BAE63B55"
			rewards: [{ id: "7499F9157AFA03AF", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [{ count: 4L, id: "3AE097BD93E618FF", item: "grindless:magnetic_bearing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Bearings"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["564E7FD4BAE63B55"]
			description: ["In orbit, neurons grow in three dimensions without a scaffold. The &6Organoid Lab&r turns stem cells, growth medium and the ring's neurotrophic factor into a neural organoid. Stem cells from the biofoundry, and factor from the ring. The neuro processing unit, in the circuits chapter. Nothing else makes one before ZPM. Feed the lab by ME and let the organoids go straight to the assembler."]
			icon: "gtceu:organoid_lab"
			id: "7C67E4A7D55ABED5"
			rewards: [{ id: "1AB884D956CE2276", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "10DDD5BEE2DAB461", item: "gtceu:organoid_lab", type: "item" }]
			title: "Organoid"
			x: 12.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C67E4A7D55ABED5"]
			description: ["A &6Neural Organoid&r is living tissue wired up in orbit. It is only as good as the factor and medium that fed it, so check them before blaming the lab."]
			icon: "grindless:neural_organoid"
			id: "31DC0512EB49BCD2"
			rewards: [{ id: "32AFFB47DC78AB47", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "52BFDE40294BD2AD", item: "grindless:neural_organoid", type: "item" }]
			title: "Neural Organoid"
			x: 14.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F943A5682742ECD"]
			description: ["The &6Optical Miner&r bags crumbly carbon-rich boulders and bakes them with mirrors until water, carbon dioxide and a nitrogen-and-phosphorus extract boil off. Capture bags and the Sun on its receiver, and the Sun is faint out here, hence all the mirrors. Chondritic extract for the algae, water for the belt and, through its second recipe, the processor's carbon monoxide. Capture bags are returned empty. Send them back by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:optical_miner"
			id: "1997FB952337C741"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "5908F6DB648D4ECB", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ id: "7F1DFD24E69DF9E1", item: "grindless:capture_bag", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "74AB7FD3082AE1C5", item: "gtceu:optical_miner", type: "item" }
				{ id: "59B83BAC6052A234", item: "grindless:capture_bag", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Sunlight on a Boulder"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 12.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["715B44AABDAFBFAE"]
			description: ["The &6Fumarole Condenser&r sits over a field of vents and catches what the gas drops as it cools: sulfur dioxide, sulfur and a sublimate with germanium in it. Radiation vault casing round it, and the wireless hatch you brought. The only germanium before ZPM, and sulfur concrete, which needs no water. Jovian bases are built from it. Send the gas to the Volcanic Intake next door and ship the rest home."]
			icon: "gtceu:fumarole_condenser"
			id: "3448ADF675EDD8E7"
			rewards: [{ id: "5E7185555C94EB4E", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "73E53DF21AF01002", item: "gtceu:fumarole_condenser", type: "item" }
